      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/postcard-2014-20140602_17211836_0424.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140602_17211836_0424&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/postcard-2014-20140602_17211836_0424.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/postcard-2014-20140602_17212897_0425.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140602_17212897_0425&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/postcard-2014-20140602_17212897_0425.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From: Loyd, To: Ruby Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Mailed From: Huron, California on March 13, 1910&lt;br&gt;
Postcard Info: Copyright 1909, By W.F. Williams&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Miss Ruby Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Pearl, Illinois&lt;br&gt;
Pike Co.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Huron, Cal. 3-12-10&lt;br&gt;
Received your card the 11th or 12th. Suppose you have got my letter by union time.&lt;br&gt;
Loyd&lt;/p&gt;</description>
